From e232f9aa1ace2712eba039b899c9718555696a82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LiBr <me@nvme0n1p.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:28:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/47] Z 6III: live view's frame jobs complete -- the frame's
 other completions

Each live-view frame is a job of four lanes (stage table 0xa02be8690;
grant sub_40D1A81C, release sub_40D1A5C8) and completes only when every
lane's stages have run; each stage waits, with no timeout, on a flag an
interrupt posts. ../z9-qemu's combined RAW pipeline raises the RSZ's A0
and C0 bits after a frame's writes, which serves one lane; live view ran
a frame or two and stopped. What the lanes wait for, and what now raises
it (z63-lv-frame-done unless noted; DECLARED, read from what the firmware
subscribes and waits for):

- lane 2, sub_40E789CC: B0..B2 bit 12 (RSZ ISR sub_40C25CE8 ->
  sub_40CB8700 -> client sub_40E6F56C -> flag 0x200000 of 0xa03d22008),
  and in mode 5 flag 0x80000 from event 0x41d0013 -- engine 0x150c's
  +0x210 bit 31, which the 0x106 ISR sub_40C1F978 passes with +0x204/
  +0x21c as event 0x41110001 to the front end's sub_410AB2F8. The
  firmware enables bit 31 in +0x20c (0xe0240048) and live view runs
  engine bits 1 and 2; bits 29/30 are bits 1/16's frame ends, so bit 31
  is read as bit 2's (z63-150c-path2-end; +0x210's W1C admits it);
- lane 1, sub_40E75790: FRECT_LV (0x151c0000, engine1518[2]) bit 27 per
  frame and bit 29 on the third frame since the gate opened and every
  fourth after (sub_40E69FB8's own count at 0xa03d26eb0);
- lane 3, sub_40E76A60: the RSZ one-shot E unit's bit 0 after it is
  enabled (0x11 to +0x10150);
- lane 0, stage 2: flag 1 of 0xa03d22008 (sub_40E75140), set on
  0x41d0001, which sub_410AB2F8 sends once it has seen +0x204 bit 2 and
  +0x210 bit 31 -- the Z 9 model's own engine150c-bit2-model, now on.
  Its bit6 model is now off: with +0x204 bit 6 present, sub_40CAE2EC
  reads unit 0x199's +0x14 (sub_40CAD5F0) and, idle, drops the whole
  event, bit 2 with it;
- lane 0, sub_40E76080: flag 0x200, set by sub_40E6DEC8 on event
  0x410b0002 when MIPU_LV's status (0x15140000 +0x44, engine151[1],
  passed by its ISR sub_40C0D7C4) has bit 3. ../z9-qemu's later
  revision (deb3a75, raw-pipeline-1514-completion-model) found the same
  bit 3 completion in the ZR image.

The sensor-mode cycle. In a long exposure this image turns capture group
0 of the 0x1508 block off and on every frame or two: sub_41169F08 stops
it (0x4116a050) while the cycle at 0xa04ce11a8 says so, the channel-0
frame callback sub_4115C5D0 counts frames and tells CaptureSequence
0x203000c, whose handler (0x40f4009c) arms the restart sub_4116A4BC,
which waits for global0 bit 7 and turns group 0 back on. The Z 9 model's
frame clock ran only while group 0 was on and restarted its period at
each enable, so neither the count nor the boundary came and group 0
stayed off. z63-sensor-vd: once capture has run, the clock keeps its
period while group 3 is on and engine 0x150c's primary path is live, and
a tick with group 0 off raises only the sensor's own events (channel bit
0, global0 bit 7). The capture events stay with group 0, and the RAW
pipeline's frame is now made on the capture tick too, with that tick's
statistics (z63-vd-statistics), owed if the last frame is not yet
acknowledged -- a frame made off the tick had no statistics and no
exposure frame end, and its job's lane 1 (sub_40E7383C) waited for ever.

These edits to ../z9-qemu's files are made by import_z9lab.py (edit 7,
nikon-z9-pixels.h now included), so the files are generated again.

Verified: frame jobs complete and are posted to the display (83 in one
run, against 2 before); MENU opens over live view and its cursor moves;
no camera error in the last runs. smoke.sh passes.

Where it stands: the photometry results read as black (see the DSP
commit), so live view runs in its long-exposure mode -- the group 0
cycle, frames in bursts at about 12 per second -- and stalls between
bursts; a half press does not yet bring live view back from the menu.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
