 static bool z63_z9lab_lane0_ack_on;
 
+/*
+ * A live-view frame's other completions. In this image a frame is a job
+ * of several lanes (stage table 0xa02bde320), and it completes only when
+ * every lane's stages have run (0x40d1aac0 polls them); each stage waits
+ * on an event a device's interrupt posts. ../z9-qemu's combined pipeline
+ * raises the RSZ's A0 bits 0/4 and C0 bits 0/3 after a frame's writes,
+ * which serves the RSZ's own lane, and live view ran one frame, then
+ * stopped: the job pool ran dry and CaptureSequence's frame watchdog
+ * ended it with error 0x40. What the other lanes wait for:
+ *
+ *   - lane 2, sub_40E789CC: an output writer's frame end, B0..B2 status
+ *     bit 12 (the RSZ ISR sub_40C25CE8 reports B to sub_40CB8700 under
+ *     the subscription 0x1000 the live-view set-up leaves at 0xa02dc48a4;
+ *     the client callback sub_40E6F56C turns it into flag 0x200000);
+ *   - lane 1, sub_40E75790: FRECT_LV (device 0x1ce, 0x151c0000, INTID
+ *     0xf8; this model's engine1518[2]) status bit 27 once a frame, and
+ *     bit 29 when a bank of four rows is done -- sub_40E69FB8 counts bit
+ *     27 modulo 4 at 0xa03d26eb0 and, when the count reaches 3, waits for
+ *     bit 29 (flag 0x800000) before flipping banks (sub_40E5F9B4). The
+ *     firmware enables both in +0x08 (0x39f00000) and clears them through
+ *     +0x0c, as for the stop bits 21/22 above;
+ *   - lane 3, sub_40E76A60: after enabling the RSZ's one-shot E unit
+ *     (0x11 to +0x10150, sub_40C26234), its status bit 0 (+0x10154,
+ *     event 0x41160002);
+ *   - lane 0, sub_40E76080 (second stage): flag 0x200 of 0xa03d22008,
+ *     which sub_40E6DEC8 sets on event 0x410b0002 when the status it is
+ *     given has bit 3. That event is MIPU_LV's (device 0x1d0, 0x15140000,
+ *     INTID 0x10e; this model's engine151[1]): its handler sub_40C0D7C4
+ *     reads +0x44, writes it back and passes it as the event's argument.
+ *     ../z9-qemu's later revision (deb3a75, raw-pipeline-1514-completion-
+ *     model) found the same bit 3 completion after the RAW-derived writes
+ *     in the ZR image.
+ *
+ * z63-lv-frame-done (default on) raises them with the frame's other bits:
+ * B0..B2 bit 12; FRECT_LV, while its gate is open, bit 27 and, on the
+ * third frame since the gate opened and every fourth after, bit 29; E bit
+ * 0 at the first frame after it is enabled; MIPU_LV bit 3, through the
+ * model's own +0x44 pending, +0x40 mask and W1C. And it makes its frames
+ * on the capture tick of the sensor's frame timing -- the tick that also
+ * delivers the frame's statistics and engine 0x150c's bit 2 -- instead of
+ * on a 33.3 ms clock of its own: the sensor-mode cycle below turns capture
+ * group 0 off and on every frame or two in a long exposure, and a RAW
+ * frame made outside a capture tick had no statistics and no exposure-
+ * module frame end, so its job's lane 1 (sub_40E7383C) waited for ever.
+ * A tick whose frame cannot be made yet -- the last one not acknowledged
+ * -- owes it (up to two), and it is made as soon as it can be.
+ * ../z9-qemu's later revision likewise gates its new DMA on that timing.
+ * DECLARED: these meanings are
+ * read from what the firmware subscribes and waits for, not measured, and
+ * bit 29's phase is the one the firmware's own counter expects. Never A
+ * bits 8/12 or B bit 8: sub_40CB8700 takes those as errors and ends the
+ * run (sub_40CBA3FC).
+ */
+static bool z63_z9lab_lv_frame_done_on = true;
+
+/*
+ * Statistics per frame. ../z9-qemu's statistics model delivers a frame of
+ * statistics 33.3 ms after the firmware acknowledged the last one, on a
+ * clock of its own, so the deliveries drift against the sensor's frames.
+ * This image pairs them: each live-view frame job's lane 1 (sub_40E7383C)
+ * waits, with no timeout, for the exposure module's end of that frame --
+ * bit (frame id % 31) of 0xa03d22020, posted from event 0x40f0008
+ * (sub_41020C74 / sub_4102F2B0 -> sub_40F57A70 -> sub_40E80BE4) -- and a
+ * frame that had no statistics never gets one. z63-vd-statistics (default
+ * on) delivers one frame of statistics on each capture tick of the sensor's
+ * frame timing (event_timing_expire), the tick that also makes the RAW
+ * frame (z63-lv-frame-done), and, when the last delivery is still
+ * unacknowledged then, as soon as it is. DECLARED: one statistics frame per
+ * captured sensor frame, which is what the firmware's per-frame bookkeeping
+ * assumes; the content is the model's, as before.
+ */
+static bool z63_z9lab_vd_statistics_on = true;
+
+
